                0.138,
                0.901,
                0.198
              ],
              "content": "Example 3 : The distribution below shows the number of wickets taken by bowlers in one-day cricket matches. Find the mean number of wickets by choosing a suitable method. What does the mean signify?"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_9_table_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.34,
            0.899,
            0.379
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :** Here, the class size varies, and the $x _ { i } \\mathrm { s }$ are large. Let us still apply the stepdeviation method with $a = 2 0 0$ and $h = 2 0$ . Then, we obtain the data as in Table 13.8."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.101,
            0.418,
            0.896,
            0.721
          ],
          "content": "| Number of wickets taken | Number of bowlers (f<sub>i</sub>) | x<sub>i</sub> | d<sub>i</sub> = x<sub>i</sub> - 200 | ui = 2d0i | u<sub>i</sub>f<sub>i</sub> |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 20 - 60 | 7 | 40 | -160 | -8 | -56 |\n| 60 - 100 | 5 | 80 | -120 | -6 | -30 |\n| 100 - 150 | 16 | 125 | -75 | -3.75 | -60 |\n| 150 - 250 | 12 | 200 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\n| 250 - 350 | 2 | 300 | 100 | 5 | 10 |\n| 350 - 450 | 3 | 400 | 200 | 10 | 30 |\n| Total | 45 |  |  |  | -106 |",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.441,
                0.391,
                0.559,
                0.409
              ],
              "content": "Table 13.8"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_9_table_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.744,
            0.858,
            0.791
          ],
          "content": "So, $\\bar{u} = \\frac{-106}{45}$ ⋅ Therefore, $\\overline{x}=200+20\\left(\\frac{-106}{45}\\right)=200-47.11=152.89.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.814,
            0.9,
            0.855
          ],
          "content": "This tells us that, on an average, the number of wickets taken by these 45 bowlers in one-day cricket is 152.89."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.869,
